1 0 0 1 0 0 cm  BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 750 Tm (Introduction) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 735 Tm (Camera traps at night rely on infrared illumination, which can disturb some animals.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 720 Tm (Event cameras report brightness changes per pixel and work at very low light levels.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 705 Tm (Their sparse output suits spiking detectors that run on low-power hardware in the field.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 690 Tm (Few studies measure how detection quality changes as the scene gets darker.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 675 Tm (We collect clips in forests and report recall at several controlled light levels.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 660 Tm (Our aim is to find the light level below which detection becomes unreliable.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 645 Tm (We also compare the power draw of the event camera with an infrared reference camera.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 630 Tm (The dataset and labels are described in the methods section of this paper.) Tj T* ET
.6 g
0 g
 
endstream
