1 0 0 1 0 0 cm  BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 750 Tm (Figure 3 shows per-species recall; the exact values appear only in the figure.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 735 Tm (Mean recall fell from 0.71 at 2 lux to 0.52 at 0.5 lux across all nine species.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 720 Tm (False positives were most often caused by moving branches in windy conditions.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 705 Tm (Recall was stable across the two recording seasons for most of the species.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 690 Tm (Small animals such as mice were detected less often than larger mammals.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 675 Tm (Detection latency on the field hardware stayed below 40 milliseconds per clip.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 660 Tm (Adding a fifth temporal bin did not change mean recall in our ablation runs.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 645 Tm (Clips with rain produced more events but did not reduce recall noticeably.) Tj T* ET
.6 g
0 g
 
endstream
